+# Volt rear-window curve — 2026-10-31
+
+RGC01 follows the owner's red guide at the lower edge of the rear window. The former forward bow is reversed into a shallow rearward arc. At the visible glass edge the centre is 184.32 mm behind the corners in authored coordinates, or **16.22 cm at car scale**. Previously it was 147.46 mm ahead. The corners stay in place, while the centre of the glass extends back over the deck.
+
+RGC02 gives the backlight a gentle transverse crown (18.43 mm at its visible lower edge) and eases the changed shape in from the existing roof seam. The glass and painted deck now share one boundary function. The deck is reshaped to meet it; its lip follows that panel. The actual tail cap remains exact. The native full/simple glass-to-deck residual is below 0.001 mm; both painted roof rails also meet the deck within the retained 0.5 mm limit. The deck retains positive depth across its width.
+
+[Matched before/after views](evidence/volt-curved-rear-window-2026-10-31/before-after.html) show the actual model from above and the rear quarter, in blue and factory silver. Six final views were captured with desktop Compatibility and six with desktop Mobile. These are model renders, with matching cameras and lighting.
+
+RGC03 retains the preceding sports hood, front glass, panoramic roof, flanks, front-wheel inset, subtle fenders and closed wheel bays. The focused actual-buffer fixture passes **32/32** full/simple checks. The exact task-start geometry fails the four rearward-curve checks and passes the other 28, showing that the new checks reject the previous boundary. The fender fixture passes 96/96, including all 120 wheel-bay rays; its former exact-rear-screen assertion is explicitly replaced by the owner's requested new curve. The front glass, roof and hood exact comparisons remain.
+
+The retained sports regression passes 104/104, including exact procedural/prepared parity for all 333 meshes. Comparing every prepared surface with the preceding model gives 323 exact meshes and ten expected changes: rear glass, two rails, deck and deck lip at both detail levels. The modular-assembly comparison passes 44/44. The actual App Garage/race fixture passes 58/58 with nine captures. Its frame-hitch output is retained and does not establish performance. Visible geometry remains within the unchanged 120,000/45,000 triangle budgets; the all-mesh regression also counts the simple model's hidden shadow proxies.
+
+Three runtime sources change: `electric_reference_body.gd`, `electric_reference_cabin.gd` and the prepared directory constant in `electric_reference_mesh.gd`. The current resources use `electric_curved_rear_window_v1`; the previous subtle-fender directory remains byte exact. Electric's two modular assemblies, Garage template, five shadow proxies and 52 preview pictures are refreshed and imported. Handling configuration, simulation, Electric resource, main car builder and detail builder remain byte exact against task start.
+
+Initial fixture runs used sanitized node names as prepared keys, causing missing side-resource errors; those test sessions were stopped and the lookup was corrected. Another initial fixture expected an exact deck lip, although the lip follows the revised deck; the final retention assertion covers the actual tail cap. A first array audit had a void-return expression error. Its corrected run exposed tiny unintended floating-point differences in the side windows; the morph now bypasses the unchanged outer corners, restoring all side-window buffers exactly. The strict ten-mesh audit passes. These findings are retained. The standard Garage baker initially reused a modular assembly and lacked the prepared-cache entry it requires (error 20); the successful offline wrapper disables modular restoration for that bake. No runtime cache code was changed.
+
+[Commands, measurements, hashes and the source checkpoint](evidence/volt-curved-rear-window-2026-10-31/report.json) record the result. Every unattended engine command uses `scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py` and an isolated offline profile. Certificate-store warnings remain in the logs. The source-only patch is checked forward and reverse with exact content, without the main index.
+
+Reload/rebuild and owner appearance acceptance remain. No physical-device query/test, APK, deployment, live/backend/owner-save mutation, owner-process restart, staging, commit or merge was performed. Desktop Mobile rendering does not measure phone performance. Concurrent work is preserved.
